WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.738
Welcome back to your Danish citizenship exam companion.

2
00:00:03.688 --> 00:00:07.080
This is Chapter Six, Episode Eighteen, Part Two.

3
00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:12.030
Smoking is the biggest single cause of illness and death in Denmark.

4
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:16.268
About 16,000 people die each year as a result of smoking.

5
00:00:16.268 --> 00:00:19.492
That is more than every fourth death in Denmark.

6
00:00:19.492 --> 00:00:31.680
To get people to smoke less, it has been forbidden to smoke indoors in public places, that is places where there is access for everyone: for example public transport, sports halls and cinemas.

7
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:39.380
It is also forbidden to smoke at workplaces and schools and in by far most restaurants, cafés, bars and discos.

8
00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:50.880
Pupils in folkeskoler and in youth educations, for example upper secondary schools and vocational schools, are forbidden to smoke during school hours, also outside the school's area.

9
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:57.755
In addition cigarettes and other tobacco must be hidden away in shops so that they cannot be seen by customers.

10
00:00:57.755 --> 00:01:10.722
In 2019, a political majority agreed to raise the price of a packet of cigarettes from about 40 kroner to 55 kroner in 2020 and further to 60 kroner in 2022.

11
00:01:11.272 --> 00:01:18.584
Furthermore, in recent years there has been increased focus on mental health and psychological disorders and illnesses.

12
00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:26.572
The Danish Health Authority's survey, "The National Health Profile", shows that the Danish population overall has good mental health.

13
00:01:26.572 --> 00:01:36.959
More and more Danes over 16 do, however, state that they have poor mental health, from 10 percent in 2010 to 17.4 percent in 2021.

14
00:01:36.959 --> 00:01:43.222
The development in poor mental health is seen especially among young people aged 16 to 24.

15
00:01:43.222 --> 00:01:58.428
Among women in this age group, the share who experience poor mental health has risen from 15.8 percent to 34.4 percent and among men from 8.3 to 21.1 percent in the period 2010 to 2021.

16
00:01:58.978 --> 00:02:00.853
The Danish health service.

17
00:02:00.803 --> 00:02:06.691
It is the regions, regionerne, that are responsible for running by far most of the health service.

18
00:02:06.691 --> 00:02:12.965
The regions run the hospitals, sygehuse; the municipalities and the state do not run hospitals.

19
00:02:12.965 --> 00:02:16.965
Police are the state's job and kindergartens the municipalities'.

20
00:02:16.965 --> 00:02:20.565
That applies to the hospitals, which are free for patients.

21
00:02:20.565 --> 00:02:37.902
And the regions give all citizens resident in the country the right to free help from a general practitioner and a specialist doctor, as well as grants towards, among other things, treatment at a physiotherapist, dentist, psychologist and the purchase of medicine at the pharmacy.

22
00:02:38.452 --> 00:02:47.639
The general practitioners, specialist doctors, physiotherapists, dentists, psychologists and others are self-employed business people.

23
00:02:47.589 --> 00:02:51.464
They are, however, paid wholly or partly by the regions.

24
00:02:51.464 --> 00:02:56.477
It is thus free to go to your general practitioner, who is the entrance to the health service.

25
00:02:56.477 --> 00:03:03.889
By far most citizens are registered with a regular general practitioner, who is also called "own doctor", egen læge.

26
00:03:03.889 --> 00:03:10.327
In most cases the general practitioner finishes the examination or treatment of a patient themself.

27
00:03:10.327 --> 00:03:26.280
But the patient can also be referred, sent on, to a specialist doctor in private practice, for example a dermatologist, surgeon, gynaecologist or neurologist, or to a hospital, if the general practitioner assesses that there is a need for it.

28
00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:31.117
In recent decades many hospitals have been closed down in Denmark.

29
00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:36.780
Instead, treatments have been gathered in far fewer, but in return bigger, hospitals.

30
00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:52.605
An important purpose of this merging is to achieve higher quality in treatment, because the doctors and nurses can get greater experience and routine with complicated treatments, and because the large hospitals can better afford to buy the newest and best equipment.

31
00:03:52.605 --> 00:04:07.194
This development has however also triggered some dissatisfaction in parts of the population, because many towns have lost their local hospital and thereby also jobs, and because a large part of the population has got a longer distance to a hospital.

32
00:04:07.744 --> 00:04:15.944
While hospitals and general practitioners are free, there are also parts of the health service where patients pay wholly or partly themselves.

33
00:04:15.894 --> 00:04:24.516
There are for example grants when you buy prescription medicine, but part of the amount, up to a limit, you must pay yourself, egenbetaling.

34
00:04:25.066 --> 00:04:30.116
As a main rule you must also pay part of the bill yourself when you go to a psychologist.

35
00:04:30.066 --> 00:04:40.854
But there is a grant for certain patients if their doctor has referred them, for example because they have been victims of a serious accident, attempted suicide or have anxiety or depression.

36
00:04:41.404 --> 00:04:48.016
Dental care, tandpleje, is free for children and young people up to and including 21 years.

37
00:04:47.966 --> 00:04:55.704
After that there are grants for certain examinations and treatments, but the patient's own payment for dental care is generally high.

38
00:04:56.254 --> 00:05:07.194
The municipalities also have responsibility for part of the health service, not least for taking care of the sick after they have been discharged from hospital, and when it comes to preventing diseases.

39
00:05:07.744 --> 00:05:26.748
It is thus the municipalities that are responsible for, among other things, care and rehabilitation after hospital admission, and also home nursing, treatment of alcohol and drug abuse, child and youth dental care, social psychiatry and prevention, including offers of help to stop smoking.

40
00:05:27.298 --> 00:05:29.860
Here is your recap for Episode Eighteen.

41
00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:34.785
The health service made up 9.4 percent of the economy in 2025.

42
00:05:34.785 --> 00:05:47.048
Life expectancy, middellevetid, was about 40 years in the 1800s; in 2024 to 2025 it is 83.9 for women and 80.3 for men.

43
00:05:47.048 --> 00:05:57.485
Average height has grown from about 165 centimetres for men and 155 for women to 180 and 167.

44
00:05:57.485 --> 00:06:02.710
Reasons: more food, medical science, hygiene, and a health service.

45
00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:18.935
Over 100 hospitals were built in the late 1800s and early 1900s; the state gave grants to sick funds from 1893; the sick funds lasted until 1973, when public health insurance replaced them.

46
00:06:18.935 --> 00:06:31.860
Lifestyle diseases include cancer, cardiovascular disease, diabetes and COPD; severe overweight rose from 5 to 6 percent in 1987 to 19 percent in 2023.

47
00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:36.448
Unskilled workers live five to seven years shorter than academics.

48
00:06:36.448 --> 00:06:52.023
You must be 16 to buy light beer, øl, of 1.2 to 6 percent and 18, atten år, for cigarettes, strong beer, wine and strong spirits, stærk spiritus; in nightlife zones 18 after 10 pm.

49
00:06:52.023 --> 00:06:57.010
Smoking kills about 16,000 a year, more than every fourth death.

50
00:06:57.010 --> 00:07:03.323
The regions run most of the health service: hospitals, free general practitioners and specialists.

51
00:07:03.323 --> 00:07:12.223
Dental care is free up to and including 21 years, and child and youth dental care is run by the municipalities, not the regions.

52
00:07:12.223 --> 00:07:25.110
The municipalities handle care and rehabilitation after hospital, home nursing, treatment of alcohol and drug abuse, child and youth dental care, social psychiatry and prevention.

53
00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:28.260
Now it is time for your exam practice.

54
00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:33.122
These are real questions from past Danish citizenship exams on what you just heard.

55
00:07:33.122 --> 00:07:40.608
For each one, I will read the question and the choices, then pause so you can pick your answer, and then I will give you the correct answer.

56
00:07:41.158 --> 00:07:42.408
Question 1.

57
00:07:42.358 --> 00:07:44.758
What are the regions responsible for running?

58
00:07:44.758 --> 00:07:46.995
Option A: The police.

59
00:07:46.995 --> 00:07:49.095
Option B: Hospitals.

60
00:07:49.095 --> 00:07:51.306
Option C: Kindergartens.
[DA] Hvad har regionerne ansvaret for at drive?  A: Politi  |  B: Sygehuse  |  C: Børnehaver

61
00:07:57.856 --> 00:08:00.231
The answer is B: Hospitals.

62
00:08:00.181 --> 00:08:04.332
It appeared in the June 2020 and June 2022 exams.
[DA] ✔ B: Sygehuse

63
00:08:04.882 --> 00:08:06.132
Question 2.

64
00:08:06.082 --> 00:08:09.182
Who has the main responsibility for running the hospitals?

65
00:08:09.182 --> 00:08:11.244
Option A: The state.

66
00:08:11.244 --> 00:08:13.457
Option B: The regions.

67
00:08:13.457 --> 00:08:16.230
Option C: The municipalities.
[DA] Hvem har hovedansvaret for driften af sygehusene?  A: Staten  |  B: Regionerne  |  C: Kommunerne

68
00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:25.280
The answer is B: The regions.

69
00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:27.912
It appeared in the May 2025 exam.
[DA] ✔ B: Regionerne

70
00:08:28.462 --> 00:08:29.799
Question 3.

71
00:08:29.749 --> 00:08:33.187
Who is responsible for running child and youth dental care?

72
00:08:33.187 --> 00:08:35.962
Option A: The municipalities.

73
00:08:35.962 --> 00:08:38.174
Option B: The regions.

74
00:08:38.174 --> 00:08:40.218
Option C: The state.
[DA] Hvem har ansvaret for driften af børne- og ungdomstandplejen?  A: Kommunerne  |  B: Regionerne  |  C: Staten

75
00:08:46.768 --> 00:08:49.680
The answer is A: The municipalities.

76
00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:52.572
It appeared in the November 2023 exam.
[DA] ✔ A: Kommunerne

77
00:08:53.122 --> 00:08:54.884
That's the end of this part.

78
00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:55.902
Well done.

